            {
               "text": "<p><span id=\"htZoomImageMsg\"></span></p><p><h3>Prerequisites</h3>In this text, we explore the concept of equality. For more details, we recommend starting with:</p><p><ul><li><b>Drawing to count</b>: show how we change from our fingers to geometric pictures (<htcite0>).</li><li><b>Our current numbers</b>: Here are the numbers we use today (<htcite1>).</li><li><b>Numerical families (Part I)</b>: Illustrating the relationship between our ancestors and numbers (<htcite2>).</li><li><b>Change of direction</b>: In this text, we examine the direction in which Indigenous peoples write their numbers (<htcite3>).</li><li><b>Numerical families (Part II)</b>: This section introduces the reader to the names of generations and numerical orders (<htcite4>).</li></ul></p>",
